# r477-r490 security-scan SKILL.md
SPLIT R:EXTRA-M-0024 | a: The security scan report contains Scope, a Limitations statement (static analysis only), a severity Summary table, Findings and Layer Results for the seven layers using PASS / FINDINGS / NOT APPLICABLE / NOT CHECKED. | b: The security scan uses the fixed severity scale Critical / High / Medium / Low / Info with defined meanings.
SD P:EXTRA-M-0187 R:EXTRA-M-0024#b | S: security scan output M: MUST both E: none in either T: at reporting
RD COMPOUND_PART R:EXTRA-M-0024#a P:EXTRA-M-0185 | R's report structure includes the Limitations statement P requires.
SPLIT R:RULE-M-0202 | a: Investigation prompts are not automatic vulnerability declarations. | b: Report concrete risks and distinguish confirmed findings from items needing verification. | c: Rate severity by exploitability, reachability, exposure and impact rather than mechanically by pattern, CVSS or OWASP category. | d: Avoid known false positives. | e: Do not claim a static scan proves design security. | f: Do not invent exploitability. | g: Do not upgrade packages during a scan unless asked.
RD COMPOUND_PART P:RULE-M-0559 R:RULE-M-0202#b | P bundles concrete risks / confirmed vs needs-verification with contextual severity.
RD COMPOUND_PART P:RULE-M-0559 R:RULE-M-0202#c | P includes the contextual-severity rule.
RD EXAMPLE_GENERAL R:RULE-M-0202#c P:RULE-M-0569 | P: do not convert advisory CVSS scores directly into application severity.
RD OVERLAP R:RULE-M-0202#c P:RULE-M-0568 | P lists the severity factors (privileges, blast radius, reliability, compensating controls).
RD OVERLAP R:RULE-M-0202#e P:EXTRA-M-0185 | R: do not claim a static scan proves security; P: the report must state that static review cannot prove security.
RD EXAMPLE_GENERAL R:RULE-M-0140#b P:RULE-M-0558 | P: read security.md before scanning.
RD EXAMPLE_GENERAL R:RULE-M-0105 P:RULE-M-0560 | P: do not suppress a real secret because it is in a Development file.
RD EXAMPLE_GENERAL R:RULE-M-0149 P:RULE-M-0561 | P: do not require security mechanisms the project does not need.
RD OVERLAP R:RULE-M-0111 P:RULE-M-0562 | P: evaluate effective authorization behavior including global/fallback policies.
SPLIT R:RULE-M-0203 | a: The security scan works without any specific MCP server, agent, analyzer, commercial scanner or external tool; tooling is evidence, never the sole authority. | b: A scanner-reported issue is reported only after inspecting the actual code and its reachability.
SD P:RULE-M-0564 R:RULE-M-0203#a | S: security scan M: MUST (P) = MUST NOT depend on tooling (R) E: none in either T: none
RD COMPOUND_PART P:RULE-M-0567 R:RULE-M-0203#b | P adds 'use available tooling' to inspecting reachability before reporting.
